---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretSymptomsResult = await interpretSymptoms(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const planDiagnosticsResult = await planDiagnostics(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretSymptomsResult.accepted);
const matchRepairersResult = await matchRepairers(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planDiagnosticsResult.accepted);
const coordinateWorkResult = await coordinateWork(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, matchRepairersResult.accepted);
const captureOutcomesResult = await captureOutcomes(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, coordinateWorkResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretSymptoms: interpretSymptomsResult, planDiagnostics: planDiagnosticsResult, matchRepairers: matchRepairersResult, coordinateWork: coordinateWorkResult, captureOutcomes: captureOutcomesResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretSymptomsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planDiagnosticsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...matchRepairersResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...coordinateWorkResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...captureOutcomesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretSymptomsResult.checks, ...planDiagnosticsResult.checks, ...matchRepairersResult.checks, ...coordinateWorkResult.checks, ...captureOutcomesResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A volunteer’s qualification expires: block assignment requiring it while retaining unrelated skills. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (block assignment requiring it while retaining unrelated skills.) through the existing stage result for RepairSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior RepairSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A donated spare part has uncertain compatibility: request evidence before use. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (request evidence before use.) through the existing stage result for RepairSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior RepairSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — The customer’s budget changes: reapprove scope before additional work. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (reapprove scope before additional work.) through the existing stage result for RepairSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior RepairSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A repair temporarily masks the symptom: keep a monitoring or recurrence record. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (keep a monitoring or recurrence record.) through the existing stage result for RepairSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior RepairSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — An item is unsafe to handle in the workshop: route it through the approved specialist process. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (route it through the approved specialist process.) through the existing stage result for RepairSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior RepairSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretSymptoms: interpretSymptomsResult, planDiagnostics: planDiagnosticsResult, matchRepairers: matchRepairersResult, coordinateWork: coordinateWorkResult, captureOutcomes: captureOutcomesResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
